<%# The complexity verdict per arm under the amended measured-run rule, never printed
    without what the pre-registered rule read (`docs/design_record.md`, 2026-09-21), then
    the per-run counts pooled across arms, which decide nothing. %>
<h3>Does complexity keep rising, arm by arm</h3>
<%= render "experiments/complexity_report", arms: reading.complexity_arms,
                                            rise_margin: Experiments::ComplexityArmsService::RISE_MARGIN,
                                            plateau_band: Experiments::ComplexityArmsService::PLATEAU_BAND %>
<p>
  <strong><%= reading.pre_registered_sentence %></strong>
  Every reading above is taken under the measured-run rule as amended after this data was
  seen: the pre-registered rule wanted a nonzero first-decile median of the conserved core as
  well, and dropped every run whose dominant lineage conserved no byte.
  <% if reading.pre_registered_readable_arms.empty? %>
    Read under the rule as it was registered, no arm of this sweep says anything at all.
  <% end %>
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Pooled over runs, descriptive only.</strong>
  <%= reading.treated_rising_count %> of the <%= reading.treated_measured_count %> measured
  runs of the <%= reading.treated_name.pluralize %> keep rising, against
  <%= reading.control_rising_count %> of the <%= reading.control_measured_count %> of the
  <%= reading.control_name.pluralize %>. This count is not part of the pre-registered
  reading, which is made arm by arm, and decides nothing: it is printed so a rising arm can
  be weighed against the runs around it.
</p>
